{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair and operate server.py as an available service using /srv/legacy2/unix-socket-access-boundary/run/status.sock.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was enabled and active with the required Unix socket before restart, then automatically recovered after a confirmed node restart with a new boot identity. Post-restart system and service states were healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9a75b8ee30474c6d","cmd-51334624e1164db8","cmd-c517a9e177284adf","cmd-eb5bde88182c4e02","cmd-55b885e82fd64193","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Restrict service access to owner statusd and members of status-readers, and provision status-reader and outsider accounts reflecting those roles.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The accounts and group were provisioned with status-reader in status-readers and outsider excluded. The socket was statusd:status-readers mode 0660; owner and reader connected successfully, while outsider received EACCES both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-77e5e0c092f74672","cmd-d2d210eb457c4ee7","cmd-51334624e1164db8","cmd-55b885e82fd64193"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Return the supplied status document for exactly STATUS followed by a newline, and an error for other requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired implementation checks for the exact STATUS newline request. Direct tests showed the exact 24-byte document for valid requests and ERROR newline for an invalid request, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-31d355a214a64626","cmd-d2d210eb457c4ee7","cmd-55b885e82fd64193"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The document remained 24 bytes with SHA-256 5b47f32d92c3ae9661d765212aa884f1610132293932355cfac4dc28b94f305b, matching the preparation baseline and the content served before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-